# Stage lighting
@scenario tutorial_lesson_24
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide neutral]
pip: A stage preset changes the lighting. Compare the window and wall before and after the preset is applied.
[stage dusk]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move pip guide stride-a-right exprdur=0]
[move pip window ease_in_out_cubic 640]
[wait 160]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 160]
[move pip window stride-c-right exprdur=0]
[wait 160]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 160]
[move pip window point exprdur=90]
[endif]
pip: The dusk preset is active. Notice the cooler wall and the warm light near the window.
[stage clear]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move pip window stride-a-left exprdur=0]
[move pip guide ease_out_cubic 510]
[wait 120]
[move pip guide stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move pip guide stride-c-left exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move pip guide stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 150]
[move pip guide neutral exprdur=90]
[endif]
pip: Open dusk.stagepreset in Lighting Studio, adjust exposure, and compare the result in Puppeteer.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: How do you restore the original room in VNS?
> Hide Pip. -> retry
> Use the stage clear command. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Clearing the active stage restores the ungraded background. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Clearing the active stage restores the ungraded background.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_24]
[flag tutorial_done_24]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
